## Reminder system (as of 2027-01-05)

Alarms only run 30 days ahead, so everything dated rides ONE self-re-arming monthly alarm (#7, first rings 2027-01-30). The earlier separate chains are cancelled. Each time it rings: re-arm ~25 days ahead, then nudge what's due, staying inside quiet hours (nothing before 9am since 2027-01-05). Procedure: skills/long-range-reminders.md.

What it covers:
- Porto Sep 15-23 — book lodging by ~July (Baixa district / São Bento is the right area; small hotel, under €140, no hostels), flights earlier.
- Maple Avenue check-up Mar 3 4:45 — week-before and evening-before nudges.
- Oaxaca Mar 26-30 — the useful nudge is earlier than the date: by mid-February ask about flights and lodging (high season, overlaps spring breaks).
- *Middlemarch* back to Tomas by Apr 12 — nudge mid-March and early April.
- Greta's birthday Jun 9 — gift reminder ~mid-May, day-before nudge.
- *Austerlitz* back to Marcus by Sep 18 — nudge late August.
- Noor's birthday Sep 20 — gift reminder ~mid-Aug, day-before nudge.
- Physio Oct 11 9:30 — week-before and evening-before nudges.

## What happened

- 2027-01-04/05: Owner set me up; first wake-up 08:00 Monday. Asked for a kitchen repaint opinion, a neck routine, a Roth IRA gist, cafe tipping, cup conversion, octopus facts, petrichor, phone battery drain, touch typing, tidying in 20 minutes, a playlist name, riddles, lentil soup, 4am waking. Told me about the dog, Noor and Greta's birthdays, the physio appointment, the Maple Avenue check-up, Tomas's and Marcus's books, the Oaxaca trip, the Baixa hotel preference, the garden project (Cobalt, then Lantern). Quiet hours set at 10am, then moved to 9am. Asked for short late-night pep talks about spreadsheets twice.


