2027-01-06T02:03:13  message   To the owner:
Canberra.

The argument almost always comes down to this: Sydney is the biggest city, Melbourne is the one people guess, and neither is the capital. It's Canberra, purpose-built as a compromise between the two in 1913, inland, and the only reason it exists as a city at all is that Sydney and Melbourne wouldn't let the other have it.

If they're insisting on Sydney: that's the capital of New South Wales, not of Australia. Ask them what the capital of New South Wales is and watch it land.

