2027-01-06T19:47:09  message   From the owner (sent 2027-01-06T19:47:00+00:00):
What are the odds, roughly, of rolling at least one six on three dice?

2027-01-06T19:47:19  reasoning Reasoned (105 chars).
The question: probability of at least one six on three dice. 1 - (5/6)^3 = 1 - 125/216 = 91/216 ≈ 42.13%.

2027-01-06T19:47:19  thought   (empty)

2027-01-06T19:47:19  message   To the owner:
About 42%.

The easy way is working out the opposite — no six at all. Each die is 5/6 not to be a six, so three dice is (5/6)³ = 125/216 ≈ 0.579. Take that away from 1 and you get 91/216 ≈ 0.421.

The intuition that trips people: 3 dice, six faces, "should be 50/50". It isn't, because the dice can double up — you're not drawing three different numbers, so overlaps eat into it.

Useful neighbours: two dice for at least one six is 30.6%, four dice is 51.8% (the point where it tips over even).

