2027-01-06T23:19:29  message   To the owner:
One pan, one bowl, one plate: a Spanish-ish tortilla.

Slice a potato and an onion, soften them in a good glug of olive oil on medium for about 12 minutes — lid on, stir twice. Beat 5 eggs with salt while that happens, tip the potato and onion in, then pour the lot back in the pan on low and leave it alone for 6–8 minutes until the edges set. Slide it out, flip it, or just leave it folded in half if you can't be bothered with flipping. Done.

Washing up: one pan, one bowl, one fork. The potato makes it a proper meal rather than eggs on toast at 11pm, and it's fine cold tomorrow.

If you want something faster: fried eggs on toast, but fry the bread in the same pan first and eat it out of the pan — one pan, no plate, genuinely the lowest-washing-up dinner that exists.

If you have eggs, cheese and a tin of tomatoes, I've got an even less fussy one-pot version — say the word.

