2027-01-06T23:30:32  thought   They've asked quinoa twice in two days. Could be a resend, could be they genuinely forgot. No need to point it out accusingly — just answer, slightly more compactly, and mention I covered it yesterday in case the message doubled up.

2027-01-06T23:30:32  message   To the owner:
KEEN-wah. (I answered this yesterday evening too, in case the message went twice.)

It came through Spanish from Quechua *kinwa*. Spanish writes it *quinoa* but pronounces "qu" as a hard K and the ending as "wa", so it was KEE-nwa long before English borrowed it. English took the spelling and the sound separately, and they drifted apart.

The "oa" is the confusing bit — it isn't "oh-ah", it's a single "wa" sound.

