Same question as last night — answering again in case the message doubled up, and shorter.

Best value: a nice terracotta pot with a cheap, hard-to-kill plant in it (pothos, snake plant, jade). The pot is the gift and it looks considered for under $15.

Safe and genuinely wanted: a small bag of good potting mix plus a decent trowel — plant people never have enough of either.

Under $10, still good: a set of plant labels with a waterproof pen.

If unsure what they already grow: a $15 gift card to a proper local nursery, not a hardware store.

