2027-01-06T23:44:25  message   To the owner:
Answered this yesterday — shorter version, and I'll flag at the end why.

Don't treat the fan as the problem; find the heat. Sort Task Manager/Activity Monitor by CPU: one process pinned near the top is the answer (usually the browser). Then the physical ones — don't let it sit on a bed or cushion, clear the dust out of the vents if it's over two years old, and set maximum processor state to 95–99% to cut the worst noise at almost no cost. Skip cooling pads and fan-control apps.

On the repeats: that's quinoa, the plant gift and now this, all arriving a second time tonight, and you've said good night twice. I'll keep answering, but if your side is resending messages, worth a look — otherwise you'll get my replies twice too.

