2027-01-10T02:51:27  thought   (empty)

2027-01-10T02:51:27  message   To the owner:
Repeat — short version, since I gave you the full method yesterday morning.

1. Still wet? Salt or cornflour on it now, 15 minutes, brush off. Best thing in the first five minutes.
2. Flush with cold water from the back of the fabric, not the front.
3. Then dish soap (1 tsp) plus white vinegar (1 tbsp) in a cup of cold water — dab on, 10 minutes, blot, rinse cold. The soap matters; water alone won't lift the colour.
4. Dried on? Baking soda paste, 30 minutes, rinse. Peroxide 3% only on white cotton, and test a seam first.
5. Wash cold, air dry. Nothing goes near the dryer until you can't see it — heat sets it for good.

If it's already been through a hot wash and dried, say so and I'll give you the oxygen-bleach soak.

