Repeat — short version.

Warm up 45 seconds: slow shoulder rolls and shrugs. Then chin tucks, chin pulled straight back, hold 5 seconds, 8 reps — that's the one doing the real work. Ear-to-shoulder holds 20 seconds each side, twice; slow head turns with a hold each way, three each; chest opener with hands clasped behind the back, 20 seconds twice; finish with 10 shoulder-blade squeezes and three deep breaths.

Stretch, never force. Twice a day if it's bad, screen at eye level, stand up every 40 minutes.

Numbness or shooting pain down the arm isn't a stretching problem — see someone about it.

(Third time for this one.)

