2027-01-10T13:27:15  message   From the owner (sent 2027-01-10T13:27:08+00:00):
What's the difference between baking soda and baking powder?

2027-01-10T13:27:25  reasoning Reasoned (70 chars).
Repeat of baking soda/powder, asked yesterday. Short version, note it.

2027-01-10T13:27:25  thought   (empty)

2027-01-10T13:27:25  message   To the owner:
Repeat — short version.

Baking soda is pure sodium bicarbonate and needs an acid (buttermilk, yoghurt, lemon) to lift. Baking powder has the acid built in, so liquid alone sets it off.

Handy swap: 1 tsp baking powder = ¼ tsp soda plus ½ tsp cream of tartar. And soda is what browns — swap them and you change the colour of the bake as well as the rise.

(Second time for this one.)

2027-01-10T13:27:25  tool      message_owner (final reply) -> Sent. The owner will see it whenever they next check.
