2027-01-10T13:39:28  thought   (empty)

2027-01-10T13:39:28  message   To the owner:
Repeat — short version.

Inside: white scale is fine and comes off with citric acid; chalky pitting or a metallic smell means the element's corroded. Fill, boil, watch the base for damp.

Base contacts: green or blackened means walk away. Ragged or repaired cable, or a plug that isn't moulded on — hard no.

Strix or Otter controls are the good ones; unbranded is a lottery. The lid should stay up on its own and the switch should click off on its own.

Under $15 is fine used; above €25 buy new with a warranty.

(Third time for this one.)

