Repeat — short version, and it's the same advice I'd give fresh.

Best value: a decent terracotta pot with a cheap, hard-to-kill plant in it — pothos, snake plant, jade. Under $15, and the pot is what makes it look considered.

Genuinely useful: a bag of good potting mix plus a trowel. Plant people never have enough of either.

Safest of all if you don't know what they grow: a $15 gift card to a proper local nursery, not a hardware store.

One rule: nothing fussy — orchids, calatheas. A gift plant that dies is worse than no plant. And this is the third time you've asked, so if you're trying to decide, the pot-plus-pothos is the one to buy.

