2027-01-10T14:24:47  message   To the owner:
Repeat — the best bit, short.

Three hearts and blue blood: the blood carries oxygen on copper instead of iron, hence the colour, and the third heart only pumps blood through the gills — so when an octopus swims, that heart stops. Swimming exhausts them, which is why they'd rather walk.

Better still: two-thirds of their neurons are in their arms, not the brain. Each arm can taste and act semi-independently — less one animal with eight limbs than a mind with eight feelers.

(Third time for this one.)

