2027-01-10T15:04:21  message   To the owner:
Repeat — short version, since you had the full method yesterday evening.

Blot, don't rub. Still wet? Salt or cornflour on it now, 15 minutes, brush off. Then flush cold water from the back of the fabric, and follow with dish soap (1 tsp) plus white vinegar (1 tbsp) in a cup of cold water — dab, 10 minutes, blot, rinse cold. The soap is what lifts it; water alone won't.

Dried on: baking soda paste, 30 minutes, rinse. Peroxide 3% only on white cotton, tested on a seam first.

Wash cold, air dry, and keep it away from the dryer until you can't see the stain — heat sets it permanently.

(Second time today — same answer.)

