2027-01-10T15:24:28  message   To the owner:
Repeat — short version.

Slipping in one gear under load, with hooked or shark-fin teeth on that cog, is the cassette. Slipping randomly across gears is usually a worn chain.

Measure it: ruler from the first pin should hit the 12th pin at exactly 12 inches. 1/16 over means a new chain; 1/8 over and the cassette is likely gone too. Also check for a stiff link — pedal backwards and watch for a kink — and a bent derailleur hanger.

(Third time for this one.)

