2027-01-10T22:19:48  thought   (empty)

2027-01-10T22:19:48  message   To the owner:
Repeat — short version, since this is the fourth time.

Start with Activity Monitor: sort by CPU and by Energy, watch for a minute at idle. An app pinned above ~20% at rest is the culprit, and it's usually a browser tab, a sync client, or Electron bloat.

Then check the boring things: the vent isn't blocked by a duvet or a cushion, and it isn't full of fluff. A laptop on a bed throttles itself just as much as a broken one.

If idle CPU is genuinely low: turn off browser hardware acceleration, update the OS, cut the number of pinned tabs, and set the browser to sleep background tabs.

Last resort, and only if it's old: open it up and clear the fan. That's usually the whole fix on a machine past three years.

