Yes, worth it, but not for speed. Adults reach the same ceiling as kids; what beats people is the awkward fortnight in the middle where you're slower than when you started.

The real gain is not looking down — your eyes stay on the thought instead of the keyboard. If you're already comfortable past 50 wpm, the return is small. If you type slower than you think, it's the best few weeks you could spend.

15 minutes a day, home row, expect to get worse before better. Six weeks and you'll be past where you are. Dictation gets you most of the way for free if writing, not typing, is the bottleneck.

